%description:
The carriers of a cell have the same number of bands: a cell's CQI reports and the history its
AMC keeps of them are sized by one of its carriers, for all of them. A gNB on two carriers of 50
and 100 bands would use the first 50 bands of the wider carrier only, without a message, or, with
the wider carrier first, read past the end of the narrower one's SINRs. Such a cell is an error
at initialization, until CQIs are kept per carrier.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 2
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 50
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1].numBands = 100
*.gnb.cellularNic.numCarriers = 2
*.gnb.cellularNic.phy.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0] carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"
*.ue[*].cellularNic.nrPhy.componentCarrierModules = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0] carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[1]"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
carrier 3.5 GHz has 100 bands, but carrier 2 GHz of the same cell has 50: carriers of unequal width in one cell are not supported
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
